Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.59,0:00:02.18,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The Queen's name is...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.64,0:00:04.19,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Maria Kisaragi.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.40,0:00:10.07,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.66,0:00:12.91,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,I-I don't know...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.35,0:00:16.91,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,The only name Lady Kisaragi \Ngoes by is Lady Kisaragi.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.36,0:00:20.67,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Our headquarters is in Kawaguchi, Saitama.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.43,0:00:26.25,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank God I know so little... \NShe'll be safe!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.25,0:00:32.43,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I see. Then can you tell me about \Nthe structure of your group?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.91,0:00:34.43,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does this guy...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.14,0:00:37.68,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}...know who the Queen is?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.57,0:00:56.49,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.33,0:02:19.02,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Let's get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.02,0:02:22.25,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Gobo-kun, I hate to trouble you, \Nbut can you give me a hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.62,0:02:24.79,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,Sure thing, for real!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.70,0:02:30.47,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The enemy is located near Kawaguchi \NStation in Kawaguchi, Saitama.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.47,0:02:34.24,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The group's leader is the Queen, \Na woman named Kisaragi.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.88,0:02:38.60,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs9\bord2\move(320,95,320,45)\3c&HFFFFFA&\c&H747574&}Queen\NMaria Kisaragi
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.76,0:02:37.32,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,She has a personal entourage \Ncalled the "Three Powers".
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.02,0:02:40.19,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The striker is Ikusa Garai.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.60,0:02:42.10,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,Three Powers
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.60,0:02:48.86,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs20\move(167,289,167,140)\frz-2\bord3}Ikusa Garai
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.74,0:02:42.79,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Supported by Meguru Tsukioka.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.22,0:02:48.86,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs18\move(390,244,390,147)\frz-2\bord3}Meguru Tsukioka
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.12,0:02:45.55,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,And Kou Kirishima is the brains.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.10,0:02:48.86,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs16\move(556,208,556,152)\frz-2\bord3}Kou Kirishima
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.97,0:02:48.52,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Under that are lower officers \Nwho work the front line,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.52,0:02:48.86,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,{\move(395,295,395,292.5)\frz4\fax-0.05\bord3}Front line
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.87,0:02:53.03,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,which includes Touya Mutsuki and \Nanother striker named Knight Kato.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.03,0:02:56.36,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,And an additional support member, Lili Kato.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.77,0:03:02.33,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,These seven are the enemy structure \Nwe've gathered from him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.33,0:03:04.79,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Touya Mutsuki and the other front line members
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.79,0:03:08.60,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,were recently promoted to replace \NHikari Ebina and Hirayama.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.60,0:03:10.66,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,So he knows barely \Nany internal information
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.66,0:03:15.12,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,and practically nothing of the \Nother members' Rights and abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.12,0:03:17.23,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,If we piece together all of our information,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.23,0:03:21.97,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,we can determine Ikusa, Meguru, \NTouya, and Knight's Prime Rights.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.97,0:03:25.56,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Gobo, can you display \Neach of their Prime Rights?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.56,0:03:26.82,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,You got it!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.56,0:03:30.52,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,So we're missing information on...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.52,0:03:35.29,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Kisaragi the Queen, Kou of the Three Powers, \Nand the front line member Lili.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.64,0:03:38.25,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We've yet to identify \Nthe Rights of these three.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.78,0:03:40.54,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,So what next?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.54,0:03:43.05,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,We've figured out their location, \Nso do we plan an attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.45,0:03:48.56,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,No. With Touya's disappearance, the Queen \Nlikely assumed they've been compromised
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.56,0:03:51.07,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,and has already either fled or set a trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.07,0:03:54.44,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,And besides, we let those \Nother members go, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.44,0:04:01.22,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,If my theory is correct, that \Nshould make her quite uneasy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.99,0:04:03.56,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.83,0:04:09.46,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,By the way, there's no such thing \Nas Stage Three, is there?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.46,0:04:11.53,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Do you guys have a back-up plan?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.53,0:04:13.40,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,That's no problem!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.88,0:04:16.60,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,The start time was announced \Nas 10:00 PM, but we've already
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.60,0:04:20.86,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,scheduled a text message to go out \Nat 9:50 PM to delay it! For real!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.25,0:04:24.03,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I figured that's why \Nyou announced a start time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.17,0:04:27.95,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,You mean he had my \Nentire plan figured out?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.95,0:04:32.75,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,So, wait... Will the Queen be pissed, \Nnow that she's been tricked?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.75,0:04:34.35,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Oh man...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.78,0:04:37.08,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,We'll split up in groups after this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.63,0:04:38.88,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.67,0:04:45.14,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Ichinose-kun, Jin-kun, Kunashiri-kun, \Ncould the three of you come with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.44,0:04:47.71,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The rest of you will wait \Nin the lobby with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.10,0:04:49.07,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.53,0:05:01.06,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Hey, Yagihashi...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.06,0:05:01.99,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Hm?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.99,0:05:05.45,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Do you know the Queen personally?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.08,0:05:09.00,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I don't know exactly who the Queen is.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.73,0:05:11.59,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's all I can say for now...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.17,0:05:16.23,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Can we really trust this guy?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.35,0:05:20.10,Default,Meguru,0,0,0,,There's no such thing \Nas the Control Right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.11,0:05:22.72,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,That was their plan...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.47,0:05:24.74,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,We're relocating.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.74,0:05:25.84,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Get everything prepared.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.74,0:05:31.67,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,{\i1}They likely used the Suspension Right \Nto freeze Knight's attack.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.65,0:05:34.11,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which means...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.76,0:05:39.38,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,It must be Tojuro Yagihashi!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.79,0:05:46.37,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You two must have had quite the reunion.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.37,0:05:48.09,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.09,0:05:50.58,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,He only got what he deserved! \NYou dummy, Kazuhiko!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.75,0:05:53.54,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Now...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.21,0:05:57.09,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Are we all set with the audio and video?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.09,0:05:58.52,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,We're good!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.92,0:06:01.41,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I'm about to tell you \Nsomething very important.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.92,0:06:18.35,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}This guy is...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.35,0:06:20.36,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Saneatsu Narita?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.77,0:06:22.57,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Saaya! Saaya!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.57,0:06:23.79,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Don't touch them!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.83,0:06:32.30,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,During the ambush operation, \Nwe were under the impression that
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.30,0:06:36.89,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,the Emperor would be defeated \Nusing Narita-kun's Parental Authority...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.63,0:06:40.30,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,But that wasn't the case, was it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.71,0:06:42.17,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.17,0:06:44.43,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,They didn't use Parental Authority?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.51,0:06:46.33,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,You see—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.33,0:06:47.61,Italics,Ryuta,0,0,0,,I'll tell them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.03,0:06:55.64,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Sane sacrificed himself to carry out a \Nstrategy with the best chance of success.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.48,0:07:01.41,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,We baited the Emperor into \Ntaking a tally that would kill all of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.11,0:07:00.61,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs19\fad(500,1)\pos(334,59)}A question for those within the 210th floor of the Emperor's tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.11,0:07:00.61,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30\fad(500,1)\pos(321,247)}Are you part of Team Saneatsu?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.41,0:07:06.17,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,He thought he won, which created an opening\N to beat him with a remote attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.74,0:07:04.86,Board,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fs50\c&H383C3B&}Die
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.42,0:07:13.15,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,To avoid being subject to the tally, \NI fused with the cells of his puppets,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.15,0:07:16.59,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,and Omi used his Rejection Right, \Nleaving the two of us to survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.72,0:07:19.83,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,But Sane and Saaya didn't...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.84,0:07:22.41,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,That idiot...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.41,0:07:24.61,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,You mean they're both dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.61,0:07:26.76,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,They're never going to wake up?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.28,0:07:29.26,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Well, that depends.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.95,0:07:30.85,Italics,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,For example,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.33,0:07:35.04,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,what if I set my Suspension Right to halt time
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.04,0:07:38.87,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,when the two of them were \Nfaced with imminent death?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.77,0:07:41.24,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Don't tell me that...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.24,0:07:42.19,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,You mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.53,0:07:45.73,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I told you, I wanted to \Nfocus on supporting everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.91,0:07:51.29,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,So the two of them are alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.95,0:07:54.16,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Yagi-chan, great job!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.16,0:07:56.03,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Get off of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.97,0:08:00.21,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Holy crap, for real.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.21,0:08:00.89,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.05,0:08:06.92,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,But whether or not \Nthey'll survive is still 50/50.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.47,0:08:10.14,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.56,0:08:13.39,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,This is a different scenario from Sato-kun's.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.72,0:08:17.35,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,In this case, the conditions \Nof Tasuketsu become an issue.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.35,0:08:20.08,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,In other words, when exactly \Nwas death established?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.60,0:08:21.98,Comp big-an8,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,112)}Man or Woman
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.92,0:08:23.54,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The Suspension Right was set \Nto activate prior to death,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.54,0:08:25.61,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,so right before midnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.00,0:08:29.91,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,If death was established exactly at midnight, \NI'd have stopped time beforehand,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.28,0:08:44.09,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,1)\bord1\3c&H0D100E&\c&HF5F7F4&\pos(320,12)}Announcement
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.28,0:08:44.09,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,1)\bord1\3c&H0D100E&\c&HF5F7F4&\pos(320,95)}Suspension
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.28,0:08:44.09,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,1)\bord1\3c&H0D100E&\c&HF5F7F4&\pos(320,172)}Establishment\N\N\N\N\NExecution
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.91,0:08:32.58,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,so they'd live even after \NI deactivate the Suspension Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.58,0:08:38.41,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,However, if death was established the moment \Nthe question was displayed at 23:58 PM,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.88,0:08:41.69,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,their predetermined death \Nwould be waiting for them
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.69,0:08:43.34,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,after I deactivate my Suspension Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.09,0:08:47.52,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Since we don't know which is true,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.52,0:08:53.10,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,deactivating my Suspension Right\N could result in their deaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.56,0:08:56.27,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,No way...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.07,0:08:59.43,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Let's do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.80,0:09:02.05,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,It means there's still hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.05,0:09:03.61,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Thanks, Yagi-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.84,0:09:08.82,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Then let's go home... together.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.69,0:09:17.28,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Whoa... The Induction Right is so cool...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.08,0:09:21.71,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's the true brains...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.94,0:09:26.27,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,By the way, what are you gonna do \Nabout that Mutsuki dude?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.27,0:09:31.89,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,He'll be leaving us soon with the \NExplosion Right I set a little bit ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.37,0:09:40.30,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Good bye, Touya Mutsuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.29,0:09:42.72,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Sweet dreams...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.91,0:09:45.83,Show Title,,0,0,0,,{\pos(492,245)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.99,0:09:49.37,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.37,0:09:51.06,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,We're relocating?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.06,0:09:54.95,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,You seem dissatisfied, Ikusa Garai.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.66,0:09:56.95,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Kou...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.95,0:09:58.99,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,Lady Kisaragi's orders are final.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.99,0:10:01.37,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,If you can't obey her wishes, then—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.37,0:10:03.33,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,I know, shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.37,0:10:07.49,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,I'm just not happy about it, that's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.70,0:10:10.18,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Same goes for you, Kou.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.55,0:10:13.58,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,As the Three Powers, we're equal, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.58,0:10:16.49,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Then why are you her closest aide?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.49,0:10:17.61,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Stop acting so special!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.26,0:10:20.54,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.79,0:10:23.84,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,I'm nothing but a useful servant.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.84,0:10:25.95,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,There's nothing special about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.95,0:10:28.80,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,You're simply misunderstanding \Nmy circumstance...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.15,0:10:34.36,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's so full of it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.76,0:10:37.76,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,{\i1}I {\i0}will{\i1} take your place one day!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.92,0:10:44.62,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,Watch out, coming through!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.45,0:10:48.87,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,S-So what's up calling me \Nover all the sudden, hag?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.87,0:10:51.30,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,It's about your loss in this battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.72,0:10:55.16,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Perhaps it couldn't be helped considering \Nyour opponent was Tojuro Yagihashi,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.16,0:10:59.39,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,but you may have had a chance \Nto win had you put in more work.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.39,0:11:01.53,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,W-Wait a second!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.53,0:11:02.88,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,Come on, I tried!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.88,0:11:05.86,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,I tried real hard! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.78,0:11:08.44,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,The results speak for themselves...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.88,0:11:13.10,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,As the first person on the front line, I trust \Nthis loss will give you better awareness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.60,0:11:15.95,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Th-Then what about Mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.22,0:11:18.92,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,As for her, I'll let it slide just this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.92,0:11:22.52,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,But I've taken your \Nlittle sister Lili in return.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.52,0:11:24.04,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,Wha—Why Lili?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.04,0:11:25.36,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Hush.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.01,0:11:29.46,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,If you want me to free her, work harder.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.52,0:11:33.13,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,You stupid hag!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.54,0:11:38.18,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,How's Lili?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.18,0:11:42.22,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,She's fine. We're still \Nkeeping her under narcosis.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.22,0:11:44.85,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,But are you sure about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.85,0:11:46.39,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,It can't be helped.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.80,0:11:50.41,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,For some reason, I can't undo \Nthe Rights of Knight and Lili.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.83,0:11:54.41,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Knight's Destruction Right is one of the \Nstrongest under the Transmutation Attribute,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.41,0:11:57.50,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,right behind the Division Right \Nand Induction Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.50,0:12:00.93,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,There's nothing I won't do \Nto keep it within our grasp.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.37,0:12:06.59,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Family-loving kids like him are best used \Nwhen threatened with hostages.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.28,0:12:10.63,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,I see. That's very convincing, indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.05,0:12:13.55,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Kou. You do understand, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.84,0:12:16.15,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,You need not worry, milady.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.48,0:12:20.50,Default,Kou,0,0,0,,We'll be the ones left standing...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.53,0:12:26.43,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,We've got all the help we need,\Nas long as we have Yagi-chan and Sudocchi.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.43,0:12:29.54,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Don't forget me! I can blow stuff up!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.54,0:12:30.90,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Shut up, antenna head.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.90,0:12:32.90,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,What's that supposed to mean?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.00,0:12:35.41,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yagihashi...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.68,0:12:37.98,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}That guy's....{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.82,0:12:41.91,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.91,0:12:43.24,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You seem lost in thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.11,0:12:46.57,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I know what you're thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.09,0:12:52.75,Flashback,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You can trust me. We're on the same team.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.45,0:12:57.07,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's way ahead of me...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.44,0:12:59.67,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's no way I can outsmart him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.97,0:13:02.82,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,What am I doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.25,0:13:05.97,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Am I... useless?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.97,0:13:07.40,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.40,0:13:08.71,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,You not feeling well?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.23,0:13:11.30,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Nah, it's nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.62,0:13:13.03,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Hey, what are you—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.03,0:13:15.28,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Don't keep it bottled up. Speak up.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.28,0:13:16.90,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,We're your elders, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.90,0:13:19.20,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Elders...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.90,0:13:22.58,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder what Kazuki would say?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.59,0:13:26.24,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I'm just feeling sad and a bit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.76,0:13:27.87,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,You used your—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.63,0:13:31.26,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Maybe you should have kept your guard up!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.26,0:13:34.58,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,You didn't resist, which means \NI'm using my Obedience Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.58,0:13:36.84,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Go ahead and let it all out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.42,0:13:41.48,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,It's not like I can fight,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.48,0:13:45.14,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,and you've got better\N strategists than me now...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.55,0:13:48.06,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Am I even needed here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.56,0:13:52.25,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,At this point, what am I to you guys?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.52,0:13:55.69,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,You're one of us, duh.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.59,0:13:58.98,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Raion, {\i1}that's{\i0} what you were so worried about?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.69,0:14:03.42,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,But I can't do anything remotely special...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.60,0:14:06.28,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,You know Saaya?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.28,0:14:07.33,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.33,0:14:08.83,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Oh yeah, her...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.20,0:14:11.11,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,She was the same as you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.33,0:14:15.24,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,She didn't possess any Rights, but \Nshe was always ready to risk it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.98,0:14:20.05,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Yet she was an important member \Nof our group until the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.00,0:14:25.85,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,There's no rhyme or reason \Nto being a true friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.21,0:14:31.02,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,I can't explain it, but you just care about \Neach other and want to be together.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.42,0:14:34.24,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,You're great just as you are, Raion.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.52,0:14:37.77,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,No rhyme or reason...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.68,0:14:40.95,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it really that simple?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.10,0:14:44.41,Flashback,Kazuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Don't ever change yourself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.34,0:14:48.54,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}You really were right...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.41,0:14:56.33,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Before, I wanted to save the world because \Nit was the only place I shared with Kazuki...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.59,0:14:58.32,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,But now...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.10,0:15:02.26,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I want to defeat the Queen, \Nand protect you guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.26,0:15:03.86,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,We know how you feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.86,0:15:04.71,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.71,0:15:06.43,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,I may be a bit timid, but—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.79,0:15:08.31,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,We're all the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.31,0:15:08.84,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Yup.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.84,0:15:09.67,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Mm-yup!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.08,0:15:11.71,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Where did you all come from?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.52,0:15:16.24,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,My dear people, I understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.24,0:15:19.28,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Your Emperor Rahatzelt shares your conviction!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.28,0:15:21.73,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I am moved by the masses!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.73,0:15:23.45,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,You're still doing that shtick?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.45,0:15:24.32,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Super lame.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.32,0:15:26.52,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,So mean... for real!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.20,0:15:32.49,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Hey guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.39,0:15:34.20,Default,All,0,0,0,,Rika!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.83,0:15:37.46,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,{\i1}They seem to be having fun...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.12,0:15:42.38,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I thought I wanted to be alone,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.38,0:15:44.48,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,so why am I tagging along with you guys?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.69,0:15:48.37,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,We all just gathered where we felt like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.46,0:15:54.81,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,You're right...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.49,0:16:00.81,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Now...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.81,0:16:04.32,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,let's begin our strategy meeting \Nto take down the Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.59,0:16:10.11,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Everything we already know, they've \Nlikely made plans to counter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.11,0:16:12.28,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.59,0:16:14.11,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Our findings are useless
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.11,0:16:17.12,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,if they've overhauled their location \Nand team structure...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.12,0:16:19.46,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,But that's only true for the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.87,0:16:22.17,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,They can't change the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.17,0:16:25.96,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The key to our recent findings \Nlies in their past.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.37,0:16:28.46,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,The past? What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.06,0:16:33.03,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,One notable factor is the member Knight Kato.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.40,0:16:37.86,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,There was a moment when he used his \NDestruction Right without declaring its name.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.86,0:16:40.73,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,So the Destruction Right doesn't\N belong to the Production Attribute.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.73,0:16:42.96,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,I'm certain it's under \Nthe Transmutation Attribute.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.96,0:16:47.94,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,So he can use his Prime Right as much as \Nhe wants without draining his stamina?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.94,0:16:49.04,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.85,0:16:55.41,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The Queen's actions so far show that she \Nassumes the current Emperor resides in Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.74,0:17:01.92,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Then why not simply annihilate Tokyo \Nitself with the Destruction Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.92,0:17:03.50,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Annihilate?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.80,0:17:05.10,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.10,0:17:07.04,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,In combination with Mutsuki's Gravity Right,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.04,0:17:09.13,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,it would have been an easy plan to execute.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.13,0:17:10.72,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,So why didn't she do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.53,0:17:16.09,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Even if we noticed and attempted to run, \Nshe could have easily stopped us.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.09,0:17:17.24,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,How?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.24,0:17:18.31,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,For example...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.31,0:17:20.13,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Use the Destruction Right to create rubble,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.13,0:17:22.25,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,the Exchange Right to send\N it to prefecture borders,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.25,0:17:26.57,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,and finally the Duplication Right \Nto physically block us from leaving Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.57,0:17:29.99,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,True. It's not flashy, but it's certainly \Nan effective countermeasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.39,0:17:32.94,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,It could have been one of her options.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.06,0:17:35.23,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Good point...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.23,0:17:39.20,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I guess it's plausible that she'd \Nuse forcible measures like that...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.20,0:17:43.30,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,She did say that she'd use whatever \Nmeans were necessary to kill us.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.30,0:17:44.92,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I could see her going to those lengths.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.92,0:17:46.91,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,So what if we reverse that logic?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.91,0:17:51.32,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,On the one hand, she could have annihilated Tokyo\Nwhile not knowing the Emperor's whereabouts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.32,0:17:56.20,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,So why would she avoid annihilating \NTokyo in the same circumstance?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.94,0:18:02.39,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,There's someone or something \Nshe doesn't want destroyed,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.39,0:18:06.89,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,and she can't annihilate Tokyo \Nwithout putting it in danger?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.89,0:18:09.07,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,It's merely a hypothesis, but yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.41,0:18:13.65,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,But how would that hypothesis \Naffect our plan at all?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.03,0:18:16.26,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We'll shut down Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.91,0:18:17.62,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.62,0:18:19.25,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Shut down Tokyo?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.25,0:18:21.00,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,I'm completely lost right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.00,0:18:22.34,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Hear us out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.34,0:18:25.50,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Let's call this something or someone "X".
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.72,0:18:29.50,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Say "X" truly does exist somewhere in Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.50,0:18:32.23,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,If Tokyo falls under the control \Nof the current Emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.23,0:18:36.68,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,that could mean handing\N over "X" to the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.53,0:18:39.61,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,And the Queen would be forced to act...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.61,0:18:41.12,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Precisely.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.12,0:18:44.88,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,This way, we can determine \Nthe probability of "X"'s existence
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.88,0:18:48.15,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,based on the Queen's actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.15,0:18:51.41,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,If "X" does exist, we keep it \Nalive, no question.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.41,0:18:53.79,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I'm personally curious as to what it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.79,0:18:56.41,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The Queen may act regardless of if "X" exists,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.95,0:19:00.58,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,but if she doesn't act at all, \Nwe can conclude "X" doesn't exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.58,0:19:03.17,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,But how will we even shut down Tokyo anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.17,0:19:05.83,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,There's no way to know the enemy's actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.19,0:19:08.67,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We only need to pretend to shut it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.67,0:19:11.47,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Our true purpose is to find out \Nwhere their headquarters is.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.26,0:19:13.59,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Shinozaki.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.59,0:19:14.80,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Souma.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.21,0:19:20.24,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We'll use your Prime Rights to monitor people \Nmoving in and out of Tokyo from the skies.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.89,0:19:22.98,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Let's materialize clouds just in case,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.98,0:19:25.73,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,and make sure the moonlight \Ndoesn't cast your shadows.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.73,0:19:29.59,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We'll limit our search to those \Nwith descriptions that match our targets.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.59,0:19:32.97,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Share the location and appearance \Nof those you check...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.97,0:19:34.37,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Itabashi Station. Male with mohawk.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.37,0:19:37.87,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,...and we'll display them with the \NPresentation Right for further monitoring.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.87,0:19:40.49,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Display Itabashi Station's mohawk dude!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.49,0:19:43.22,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I see. It's possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.22,0:19:45.79,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Then we can let them roam free \Nback to headquarters,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.79,0:19:49.60,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,and we may not just find their \Nlocation, but the Queen herself!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.60,0:19:53.85,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Hang on. Do you think they'll even \Nbelieve that we shut down Tokyo?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.85,0:19:54.97,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Probably.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.69,0:19:58.59,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You've shown your Materialization Right \Nto the Three Powers, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.59,0:19:59.55,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.55,0:20:04.02,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Mutsuki mentioned that the Queen \Ninformed him of the Response Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.02,0:20:07.44,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,If the Queen is knowledgeable \Nabout the Rights, she must realize
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.44,0:20:10.40,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,that we can do practically anything \Nwith the Materialization Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.40,0:20:14.41,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Still, I can only materialize \Nthree times a day max.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.41,0:20:16.99,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I doubt they'd believe \Nwe can shut down Tokyo—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.99,0:20:19.36,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Actually, I don't think they know that part.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.26,0:20:23.25,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,That Meguru chick knew \Nabout the Rejection Right,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.25,0:20:27.14,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,but didn't know its effects last 72 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.14,0:20:29.33,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,That's how she fell for my trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.33,0:20:32.72,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Good point. \NThe Queen's knowledge is still limited.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.72,0:20:36.55,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,She likely knows about different \NRights and their basic abilities,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.55,0:20:39.24,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,but not in too much in detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.12,0:20:43.30,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I'm starting to get {\i1}confused{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.64,0:20:46.72,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,We just need to convince them \Nwe can, that's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.17,0:20:49.77,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Just like we don't know \Ntheir plans and intentions,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.77,0:20:52.77,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,they're in the dark about us, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.77,0:20:54.35,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Let's leverage that.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.80,0:20:58.43,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,In order to maintain the upper hand, \Nwe'll have to bluff a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.61,0:21:03.01,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We'll call it the Tokyo Blockade Operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.01,0:21:04.51,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,The plan will commence tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.10,0:21:06.87,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,We'll announce our blockade,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.87,0:21:09.83,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,and Souma and Shinozaki will \Nmonitor the ground from the skies.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.30,0:21:15.20,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Subjects will be monitored until \Nwe identify the enemy's headquarters.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.20,0:21:16.84,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,Then we'll ambush them, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.84,0:21:19.84,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,Team
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.23,0:21:18.50,Default,Sudo,0,0,0,,...take them down!
